
  <main id="main">
    <section class="page-head">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <span class="eyebrow">Terms &amp; deposit</span>
        <h1>How our projects work.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A plain-language summary of how Re-Charge projects, deposits, hosting and ownership work, so there are no surprises.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="padding-top:0.5rem">
      <div class="container container--narrow legal">
        <p class="updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>
        <p class="note"><strong>Please note:</strong> this is a plain-language summary of how we work, not final legal terms. Formal Terms &amp; Conditions will be provided with your quotation and take precedence. If anything here is unclear, ask before you pay a deposit.</p>

        <h2>1. Projects &amp; scope</h2>
        <p>Every project has a <strong>fixed scope</strong> agreed in writing before development begins. The scope lists what's included, the number of revision rounds and the delivery expectation. Anything not in the scope is a change request.</p>

        <h2>2. The R500 deposit</h2>
        <p>The R500 project deposit starts the review process and is <strong>credited toward your final project price</strong>. Paying it does not automatically accept the project at the indicative estimate — we review your requirements and confirm the final scope, price and timeline first.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>If we take the project on, the deposit comes off your total.</li>
          <li>If we're unable to take the project on after review, the deposit is <strong>refunded</strong>.</li>
          <li>For larger projects, a percentage deposit (generally 30–50%) may apply instead, confirmed in your quote.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Payment</h2>
        <p>After the deposit, the remaining balance is due as set out in your quote — typically before final handover for standard projects, or split across milestones for larger ones. Development on each stage begins once its payment terms are met.</p>

        <h2>4. Refunds</h2>
        <p>The deposit is refundable if we decline the project. Once development has started, amounts already paid cover work already done and are generally non-refundable, except where required by the Consumer Protection Act. If a problem arises, talk to us — we'll always try to find a fair outcome.</p>

        <h2>5. Revisions &amp; changes</h2>
        <p>Each project includes a defined number of revision rounds. Feedback is best given in one batch per round. Work beyond the agreed revisions, or outside the original scope, is quoted as a change request and only done once you approve it.</p>

        <h2>6. Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>To keep delivery fast, you agree to provide the content, images, access and information the project needs, and to give feedback within a reasonable time. Delays caused by missing content or feedback can move the delivery date; we'll always tell you when something is holding things up.</p>

        <h2>7. Third-party services &amp; AI usage</h2>
        <p>Domains, paid software, payment providers and AI/API usage are third-party costs. They're identified up front and either paid directly by you or added as a clearly defined cost. <strong>AI/API usage is billed on actual usage</strong> and is never included as "unlimited" in a fixed price.</p>

        <h2>8. Domains, hosting &amp; ownership</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>You own your domain.</strong> We can manage the technical side, but you remain the rightful registrant and can transfer the domain away if you leave.</li>
          <li>Hosting and Care plans are billed yearly and can be cancelled; on cancellation we help you move to another provider.</li>
          <li>On full payment, you own the delivered solution and your data. Re-Charge retains the right to reuse its own generic, non-client-specific components, templates and know-how.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>9. Hosting &amp; Care plans</h2>
        <p>Care plans cover small content updates and technical maintenance within the stated allowance. New pages, new functionality, redesigns and integrations are quoted separately. Unused time doesn't roll over between quarters.</p>

        <h2>10. Warranty &amp; support</h2>
        <p>We fix genuine bugs in delivered work at no charge for a reasonable period after launch. Changes in third-party services, new feature requests and content changes are handled under a Care plan or quoted separately.</p>

        <h2>11. Cancellation &amp; abandoned projects</h2>
        <p>You can cancel a project at any time; amounts covering completed work are payable, and the deposit is handled per section 2. If a project goes silent for an extended period without response, we may pause or close it and invoice for work completed.</p>

        <h2>12. Portfolio use</h2>
        <p>We may show finished work in our portfolio unless you ask us not to. We never publish your confidential business data, and clearly labelled demo/concept work is never presented as a real client project.</p>

        <h2>13. Privacy</h2>
        <p>Information and files you submit are used only to review and deliver your project. Uploads are validated and size-limited, submissions are protected in transit (HTTPS), and project information is kept out of search engines. See how we handle data before relying on it for confidential material.</p>

